1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:02,687
(Howard:)What would Summer Glau
be doing riding the train?

2
00:00:02,853 --> 00:00:07,103
(Leonard:)Maybe John Connor's aboard and she's
protecting him from an evil Terminator.

3
00:00:07,274 --> 00:00:09,904
(Sheldon:)Unlikely.
That's a television show, Leonard.

4
00:00:10,652 --> 00:00:12,112
(Leonard:)Thank you.

5
00:00:12,446 --> 00:00:17,286
If Skynet did exist in the future, a perfect
way to infiltrate and destroy mankind...

6
00:00:17,451 --> 00:00:19,701
(Sheldon:)...would be to send Terminators back
as actors...

7
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:22,540
(Sheldon:)...who have played Terminators
in films and television...

8
00:00:22,706 --> 00:00:25,046
(Sheldon:)...lulling us into a false sense
of security, i.e.:

9
00:00:25,209 --> 00:00:27,629
"That's Summer Glau
from The Sarah Connor Chronicles.

10
00:00:27,795 --> 00:00:30,175
(Sheldon:)No, Summer, don't kill me!
I'm pro-robot."

11
00:00:30,381 --> 00:00:32,091
[GROANING]

12
00:00:33,759 --> 00:00:36,049
(Leonard:)At least he's off the train crap.

13
00:00:37,137 --> 00:00:38,347
[TRAIN STARTING]

14
00:00:38,555 --> 00:00:39,935
SHELDON:
Wheeee.

15
00:00:41,141 --> 00:00:42,561
(Howard:)Sheldon, I owe you an apology.

16
00:00:42,726 --> 00:00:46,976
(Howard:)Taking the train was a stroke of brilliance.
I've actually got a shot at a Terminator.

17
00:00:47,147 --> 00:00:48,977
Please. When it comes to Terminators...

18
00:00:49,149 --> 00:00:52,359
(Raj:)...you've got a better shot of scoring
with Arnold Schwarzenegger.

19
00:00:53,737 --> 00:00:55,157
(Howard:)You're overlooking something.

20
00:00:55,322 --> 00:01:00,022
(Howard:)I have 11 hours with her
in a confined space.

